                <pb facs="0638" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/144.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-04-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 18, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Leishman says he has no details, but the two Americans killed at Adana were
                    named Maury and Rodgers. Says situation at Adana is improved.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
